      "text": "Good morning, and thank you for the invitation to present at this extremely important conference with official intelligence access with old playing playing and with regard to the old, the old is new again. So what is aging? Aging is a process which can, the emphasis on can, not will, bring about changes in older persons, so reducing their ability to function to the maximum. But equally older persons are protective of their independence, their right to choice, and they want to age in place. So who are older adults? The Jamaican situation is one that we have to take note of. We are moving from just under 265,000 persons in 2001 to 375,000 persons know 2021. PIOJ also predicts that by 2030, which is around the corner, we will have over 500,000 persons over the age of 60.",
