      "text": "One in four will be in fact over 60. It's also important to note the under 15 population, which over that time period has decreased from 32.5% to 21%. And this raises questions about caregiving and support. In all of this, we have to pay attention to the fastest growing age group and that's the over 80. We are moving from 49,000 to 90,000 persons for the period under discussion. So this increase in the ageing population will bring, has brought, a significant impact on society and healthcare systems. When the older adults get older, their cognitive, physical, and sensory impairments will increase. Not necessarily to the point of dementia, but we get a little forgetful.",
