      "text": "as well as the quality of life and the independence of older adults. Older adults, as I said previously, want to live alone. Well, I shouldn't say that I live alone. They want to live independently. The number one issue raised by older persons in all of our surveys dating back to 1989 is loneliness. Some live alone and are not lonely, but you have others that are lonely. And that is more important to an older person than either health or finance. So, you have many different technologies, many different AI's that have been introduced to provide older people with assistance in daily activities. Computers remind you of appointments. The internet allows you to search. Digital healthcare technology is invaluable. You will notice no persons walking around with a little wrong thing on their arm.",
