      "text": "It's monitoring their blood sugar, so you don't have problems with either excesses of high or low. Technology is now believed to be able to resolve the gap between older persons wishes and their needs. And it has great potential once we accept it and once we make sure older people accept it to assist and prolong older persons independent living. And then, as another benefit, it can help improve mental, as well as physical health and increase well-being. Voice-activated devices like Alexa, Siri and Google assist, where necessary and when necessary are easy to use because they provide hands-free assistance for persons with mobility and cardiovascular issues. You just turn around and ask Siri or Google for whatever you want. What time is it? Tell me what to do.",
